/-!
# A finite relative program from the decreased boundary reaches a nef end

Let `(X_i, B_i, Z_i, f_i, f_i⁺)_{i ≥ 0}` be a stabilized small klt tail of fourfolds, fix `i`,
and let `(p_i, Θ_i)`, `p_i : Y_i ⟶ X_i`, be a crepant junction of `(X_i, B_i)` extracting the
stable low-discrepancy set `I_∞`, with decreased boundary `Θ_i'`. Then there is a finite relative
program over `Z_i` (via `f_i ∘ p_i`) from `(Y_i, Θ_i')` all of whose models `(V_k, Θ_k)` are klt
and whose end `(V_m, Θ_m)` has `K_{V_m} + Θ_m` nef over `Z_i`. It is the
`(K_{Y_i} + Θ_i')`-MMP over `Z_i` with scaling of a small relatively ample divisor; it terminates
by the termination of birational fourfold programs with scaling, and it cannot end in a Mori
fibre space since every model is birational to `Z_i`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.StabilizedSmallKltTail.IsDecreasedBoundary.exists_relativeFourfoldProgram`:
  the program exists, for any canonical divisor `K` of `Y_i` with which it is run.

## Implementation notes

The program is run with a canonical divisor `K` of `Y_i`, which the structure
`MMP.Fourfold.RelativeFourfoldProgram` carries; the statement holds for every choice of `K`.
The models of a program are `V_k` for `k ≤ m`; the data indexed beyond `m` are unconstrained,
so klt is asserted for `k ≤ m` only.

## References

* [OpenAI, *Termination for projective log canonical fourfolds with rational boundary*][oai4]
-/

